# Reference: Agrippina Vaganova, "Basic Principles of Classical Ballet" (First Position Demi-Plié)
# Reference: Royal Academy of Dance (RAD) Classical Ballet Syllabus
# Review status: Experimental (ballet UAT; pending peer review with dance-domain educator)
# Biomechanical note: In classical first position demi-plié, turnout is initiated and held at the hips
# (~30° external rotation in base pose). Knees flex in line with the turned-out feet while both heels
# remain anchored to the floor. Under the conservative general ROM profile (15° ankle dorsiflexion ceiling),
# deep pliés (>45° knee flexion) trigger a grounding-rom-conflict diagnostic unless evaluated under
# a domain dancer profile with 25°–35° weight-bearing dorsiflexion.

posecode exercise "Demi-plié"
  rig humanoid
  pose start = first-position

  step "Plié" 2.2s settle:
    hips: flex 31.5
    hips: abduct 17
    knees: flex 55
    ankles: dorsiflex 15
    shoulders: abduct 70
    elbows: flex 15
    spine: extend 4
    ground-lock: feet
    cue "Lower straight down with knees tracking over turned-out toes, heels anchored to the floor"

  step "Straighten" 2.2s settle:
    hips: flex 0
    hips: abduct 0
    knees: flex 0
    ankles: dorsiflex 0
    shoulders: abduct 70
    elbows: flex 15
    spine: extend 4
    ground-lock: feet
    cue "Press the floor away to rise to first position, sustaining turnout and arms in second"

  repeat 4
